":"MCTM-040760","Abbreviation_in_the_article":1,"Cell_line":"HEK293","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":">50","IC50_Dark_value":50,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1021/acs.inorgchem.3c03801","Year":2024,"Counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-040760","value":"27.23 ± 1.23","numeric":27.23}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":1,"value":0.39,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"Tris-HCl buffer + NaCl","pH":7.2,"doi":"10.1021/acs.inorgchem.3c03801","year":2024,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-003799","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The partition coefficient was determined by the shake-flask method. The ligand or appropriate complex was first dissolved in one drop of DMSO and then in aqueous Tris-HCl/NaCl buffer (pH 7.2), and the initial concentration was then measured spectrophotometrically. The solution was mixed with an equal volume of saturated n-octanol, shaken for 96 h using an automated shaker, and allowed to stand for 1 h. The concentrations of the compound in the n-octanol and aqueous layers were calculated based on Lambert–Beer’s law and expressed as log P, according to eq 1 (58) log𝑃=log(𝐶octanol)/(𝐶buffer). Where Coctanol is the concentration of the analyzed compound in n-octanol and Cbuffer is the concentration of the analyzed compound in the buffer solution."}]}